+issueNumber: MDL-89296
+notes:
+  core:
+    - message: >-
+        A new standard API, \core\output\react_mount::render(), mounts React components
+        from PHP. Pass the component identifier and props, and optionally inner content
+        and attributes. Prop serialisation, escaping and the data-react-* DOM contract
+        are handled internally.
+      type: added
+    - message: >-
+        A new \core\output\react_renderable interface allows renderables to be rendered
+        as React component mount points by renderer_base::render(). It takes precedence
+        over named_templatable and templatable, but not over a render_[renderable_name]
+        method.
+      type: added
